From 88d027de8ca89934b98193169eb7b0caee5721a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weijie Gao <weijie.gao@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Jan 2021 11:26:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] board: mediatek: add upgrading/booting framework

Add framework for mediatek-specific upgrading and booting purpose:

Bootmenus:
bootmenu_mmc: generic bootmenu for eMMC and SD card
bootmenu_mtd: generic bootmenu for SPI-NOR and NAND (UBI)

Helpers:
load_data: API for loading data into DRAM
upgrade_helper: API for reading/writing various flashes
boot_helper: API for booting image from various flashes
verify_helper: API for verifying image from memory and from flash
dual_boot: API for dual-image support
bl2_helper: API for validating BL2
fip_helper: API for validating and modifying FIP
mmc_helper: API for mmc devices including dual-image
mtd_helper: API for mtd devices including dual-image

Commands:
cmd_mtkload: load data into DRAM, and optionally boot the image data
cmd_mtkupgrade: load and write data to flash region defined by the board
cmd_mtkboardboot: boot image defined by the board
cmd_mtkautoboot: display bootmenu defined by the board

To use cmd_mtkupgrade/cmd_mtkboardboot/cmd_mtkautoboot, the boards must
enable corresponding configs.

Signed-off-by: Weijie Gao <weijie.gao@mediatek.com>
